-- STEP 65 (APPLIED 2026-10-21): maps the free-text field of Masters programmes onto the filter fields (220 rows; 'Top-up' and 'Other' left as they were), and removes the sentence "Never pay anyone to apply." from the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program criteria.
-- Mapping: Agriculture and Natural Sciences->Agriculture; Allied Health Sciences, Basic and Biomedical Sciences, Environment and Health, Medical Sciences, Nursing and Midwifery, Pharmacy, Public Health->Health; Applied Sciences and Mathematics Education, Business Education, Education and Communication Sciences, Home Economics, Science Education, Technical Education, Vocational Education->Education; Chemical and Biochemical Sciences, Environment, Environment and Life Sciences, Mathematical Sciences, Mathematics, Physical Sciences, Statistics->Science; Communication, Creative Arts, Languages->Arts; Computer Science, Computing and Information Sciences, Information and Communication Technology, IT->Computing; Economics, Integrated Development Studies, Planning and Land Management, Public Policy and Governance, Security, Social Science and Arts->Social Sciences; Economics and Finance->Business; Mining->Engineering.
-- To redo: update public.programs p set field = m.new from (values ...) m(old, new) where p.level = 'Masters' and p.field = m.old;
update public.scholarships set criteria = replace(criteria, 'Never pay anyone to apply. ', '') where name = 'Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program';
